{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-14T21:52:09.006Z","data":{"text":"Task 2 is complete.\n\n**Summary of work:**\n\n1. **`AutoSteerRecord` gains `pid`** — read only when it is a number, written only when set (after `at`), so a record without a pid reads and writes byte-for-byte as before.\n\n2. **New `src/watcher/planner-spawn.ts`** — `RunContext`, `decideOutcome`, `spawnPlanner` (and `OutcomeFields`) moved out of `auto-steer-run.ts` and exported; `executeRun` imports them and its `running` record now carries `pid: process.pid`.\n\n3. **`runAutoSteer`** returns null (no spawn, no write) when the current-key `running` record has a live pid; any other `running` record is rewritten as interrupted exactly as before.\n\n4. **New `src/core/run/plan-run-record.ts`** — `planRunRecordPath`, `readPlanRunRecord`, `writePlanRunRecord`, `currentPlanRun`, `readLivePlanner` plus `PlanRunRecord`/`PlanRunView`, reusing `currentAutoSteer`, `hashChangeFolder`, `isProcessAlive`, with no watcher or `next-step.ts` import and no file writes.\n\n5. **New tests** — `tests/plan-run-record.test.ts` (4 scenarios) and `tests/auto-steer-live.test.ts` (2 scenarios); `tests/auto-steer-run.test.ts` passes unchanged.\n\nVerification: task verify 19/19 passed, and the proposal's `pnpm verify` passed (215 tests, both typechecks, build, lint). Result written to `openspec/changes/194-start-planning-button/.run/results/2.md`. Two small deviations noted there: doc comments added to the moved functions, `OutcomeFields` exported for declaration emit, and a `plannerStillRunning` helper to keep `runAutoSteer` within the 80-line function budget."}}
